{
  "duration": 76.879,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.379,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.819,
      "end": 3.319,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.759,
      "end": 7.759,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are given that a train is one hundred eighty meter long,"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.239,
      "end": 10.619,
      "text": "and it is running at fifty-four kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.279,
      "end": 12.719,
      "text": "The train crosses a pole."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.179,
      "end": 16.259,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find how many seconds it takes."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.799,
      "end": 17.719,
      "text": "Now before solving,"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.159,
      "end": 19.92,
      "text": "let us understand one"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.26,
      "end": 21.399,
      "text": "simple concept."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.92,
      "end": 23.679,
      "text": "When a train crosses a pole,"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.239,
      "end": 26.359,
      "text": "the pole has almost no width to cover,"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.979,
      "end": 29.599,
      "text": "so the train only has to cover its own length."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.959,
      "end": 31.639,
      "text": "Now let us write the given values."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.139,
      "end": 34.919,
      "text": "Length of the train is one hundred eighty meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.559,
      "end": 38.319,
      "text": "Speed of the train is fifty-four kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.84,
      "end": 39.459,
      "text": "So first,"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.86,
      "end": 42.179,
      "text": "we should convert the speed into meter per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.659,
      "end": 48.279,
      "text": "We know that one kilometer per hour is equal to five by eighteen meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.719,
      "end": 54.719,
      "text": "So fifty-four into five by eighteen gives us fifteen meters per second. Now this part is completed."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.139,
      "end": 57.239,
      "text": "We already know the distance and the speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.68,
      "end": 58.999,
      "text": "So let us use the formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.5,
      "end": 62.02,
      "text": "Time is equal to distance divided by speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.599,
      "end": 67.019,
      "text": "Putting the values, time is equal to one hundred eighty divided by fifteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.68,
      "end": 68.9,
      "text": "After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.36,
      "end": 70.419,
      "text": "we get twelve seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.9,
      "end": 74.319,
      "text": "So the train takes twelve seconds to cross the pole. Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.739,
      "end": 76.879,
      "text": "the correct answer is option C."
    }
  ],
